<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW3-QA-B3>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW3-QA-B3" ;
  triage:title "CLI timeline/merged queries bypass the documented GET /v1/diagnostics daemon route and query the store in-process" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1182-r1 (msg 01M1QSQWFKBENPSW4ZP83SKMYS) at 199a3bfeb: req-qa ATM-QA-102: sprint-AW.3 D2 specifies timeline queries go through GET /v1/diagnostics on the daemon (capability-authenticated, same as /v1/health). The CLI instead calls atm_daemon_bootstrap::assemble_default_runtime() and queries the store in-process, never issuing an HTTP request. The route implementation in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/diagnostics_route.rs is correct and unaffected. Fix: route timeline and merged through the daemon HTTP client path (atm-daemon-client) like other daemon-backed CLI commands. CLOSURE (qa-pr1182-r2, quality-mgr): b41b1fcdb's timeline_records() now calls atm_http_runtime::loopback_tcp_get_json against /v1/diagnostics through the authenticated loopback client (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/loopback_read.rs), not atm_daemon_bootstrap::assemble_default_runtime(). Independently confirmed by req-qa and arch-qa; quality-mgr read log.rs:220-227 and loopback_read.rs directly. Finding closed." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "cli-log-query" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
